Read-aloud app (installed by setup.ps1)
---------------------------------------

Piper 2023.11.14-2, https://github.com/rhasspy/piper
  MIT License. Its Windows release bundles espeak-ng (GPL-3.0),
  piper-phonemize (MIT License) and ONNX Runtime (MIT License); piper.exe
  runs as a separate process.

Piper voices, https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices
  Each voice has a MODEL_CARD with the license of its training data. The
  ones setup.ps1 knows:
  - es_MX-claude-high: Apache-2.0.
  - es_MX-ald-medium: Unlicense.
  - es_ES-davefx-medium: CC0.
  - en_US-lessac-high: trained on the Lessac Blizzard 2013 data, which
    Voice Factory International and Lessac
    Technologies release under a research licence. Check its terms before
    any other use, or choose a different English voice (VoiceEn in
    config/settings.psd1).
  - en_US-amy-medium: see its MODEL_CARD.
  - en_GB-alba-medium: CC BY 4.0.


Custom voice (voz_personalizada/, optional)
-------------------------------------------

Qwen3-TTS, https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS
  Code (qwen-tts) and models (Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base,
  Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz): Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 The Alibaba Qwen
  team. voz_personalizada/proceso_qwen/11b_entrenar_qwen.py follows the
  method of the official fine-tuning recipe (finetuning/sft_12hz.py,
  commit 022e286) and reimplements it with the corrections described in
  that file; it does not copy the recipe's code.

Qwen3-ASR-1.7B, https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-ASR
  Apache-2.0.

Whisper large-v3, https://github.com/openai/whisper
  MIT License.

PEFT, https://github.com/huggingface/peft
  Apache-2.0.

PyTorch and torchaudio, https://pytorch.org
  BSD-style licenses (torchaudio: BSD-2-Clause). The WavLM Large and
  TorchAudio-SQUIM models come through torchaudio; see its documentation.

SpeechBrain and spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb, https://speechbrain.github.io
  Apache-2.0.

wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-spanish,
https://huggingface.co/jonatasgrosman/wav2vec2-large-xlsr-53-spanish
  Apache-2.0.

python-audio-separator, https://github.com/nomadkaraoke/python-audio-separator
  MIT License. Each separation model keeps the license on its model card.

uv, https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
  MIT License or Apache-2.0.

